<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1997</h1><p class="ref-lede">1997 in world history: 10 events, 10 deaths and 2 states that came to an end. 190 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1993">1993</a><a href="/years/1994">1994</a><a href="/years/1995">1995</a><a href="/years/1996">1996</a><a href="/years/1997" aria-current="page">1997</a><a href="/years/1998">1998</a><a href="/years/1999">1999</a><a href="/years/2000">2000</a><a href="/years/2001">2001</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-22">22 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Scientists announce Dolly the sheep, the first clone of an adult mammal</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Researchers at the Roslin Institute near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a> revealed they had cloned a sheep from an adult cell. Dolly, born in July 1996, sparked worldwide debate on the ethics of cloning.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-30">30 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Britain hands Hong Kong back to China</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At midnight, at a ceremony attended by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a> and President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiang-zemin">Jiang Zemin</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> after 156 years of British rule. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a> became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/special-administrative-regions-of-china">Special Administrative Region</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-1">1 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Britain hands Hong Kong back to China</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At midnight <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a> passed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, ending 156 years of British rule. The territory became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/special-administrative-regions-of-china">Special Administrative Region</a> under the 'one country, two systems' principle.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-4">4 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mars Pathfinder lands on Mars</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">NASA's Pathfinder bounced to a landing on airbags in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ares">Ares</a> Vallis and soon deployed Sojourner, the first rover on another planet. The mission returned thousands of images and revived public interest in Mars.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-12">12 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Malala Yousafzai is born in Pakistan's Swat Valley</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Malala Yousafzai was born in Mingora. Shot by the Taliban in 2012 for campaigning for girls' education, she survived and in 2014 became the youngest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> laureate.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-15">15 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Gianni Versace is shot dead outside his Miami Beach home</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Fashion designer Gianni Versace was murdered on the steps of his villa by Andrew Cunanan, who had already killed four men. Cunanan killed himself eight days later as police closed in.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/paris" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-31">31 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Diana, Princess of Wales dies in a Paris car crash</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Diana was fatally injured when her car crashed in the Pont de l'Alma tunnel while pursued by photographers. Her death provoked an extraordinary outpouring of public grief in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and beyond.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/handover-of-hong-kong">Handover of Hong Kong</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Handover of Hong Kong was the transfer of sovereignty over Hong Kong from the United Kingdom to the People's Republic of China in 1997.</p></div></li></ol></section>
